00:00:00.460 --> 00:00:05.340
So far, the classification examples we've talked about have used binary classification

00:00:05.340 --> 00:00:10.700
where you had two possible labels, 0 or 1. Is it a cat or is it not a cat? What if you

00:00:10.700 --> 00:00:15.700
have multiple possible classes? There's a generalization of logistic regression called

00:00:15.700 --> 00:00:21.080
softmax regression that lets you make predictions where you're trying to recognize one of C

00:00:21.080 --> 00:00:27.380
or one of multiple classes rather than just recognize two classes. Let's take a look.

00:00:27.380 --> 00:00:31.740
Let's say that instead of just recognizing cats, you want to recognize cats, dogs, and

00:00:31.740 --> 00:00:38.660
baby chicks. So I'm going to call cats class 1, dogs class 2, baby chicks class 3, and

00:00:38.660 --> 00:00:43.460
if none of the above, then there's an other or none of the above class, which I'm going

00:00:43.460 --> 00:00:50.060
to call class 0. So here's an example of the images and the classes they belong to. That's

00:00:50.060 --> 00:00:56.060
a picture of a baby chick. So the class is 3, cats is class 1, a dog is class 2. That's

00:00:56.820 --> 00:01:03.820
a koala. So that's a none of the above. So that's class 0, class 3, and so on. So the

00:01:03.820 --> 00:01:11.060
notation we're going to use is I'm going to use capital C to denote the number of classes

00:01:11.060 --> 00:01:16.940
you're trying to categorize your inputs into. And in this case, you have four possible classes,

00:01:16.940 --> 00:01:22.740
including the other or the none of the above class. So when you have four classes, the

00:01:22.740 --> 00:01:29.740
classes indexing your classes will be 0 through C minus 1 through capital C minus 1. So in

00:01:29.740 --> 00:01:33.300
other words, it will be 0, 1, 2, or 3. In this case, we're going to build a neural network

00:01:33.300 --> 00:01:41.300
where the output layer has 4, or in this case, the variable capital alphabet C output

00:01:41.340 --> 00:01:48.340
units. So n, the number of units in the output layer, which is there L, is going

00:01:49.260 --> 00:01:55.220
to be equal to 4, or more generally is going to be equal to C. And what we want is for the

00:01:55.220 --> 00:01:59.460
number of units in the output layer to tell us what is the probability of each of these

00:01:59.460 --> 00:02:06.460
four classes. So the first node here is supposed to output, or we wanted to output, the probability

00:02:06.620 --> 00:02:12.140
that is the other class, given the input x, this will output probability that is a cat

00:02:12.700 --> 00:02:19.700
given x, this will output probability that is a dog given x, that will output the probability,

00:02:19.940 --> 00:02:25.780
I'm just going to abbreviate baby chick to be BC. So probably have a baby chick abbreviated

00:02:25.780 --> 00:02:32.780
BC, given the input x. So here, the output labels y hat is going to be a four by one

00:02:35.300 --> 00:02:40.740
dimensional vector, because it now has to output four numbers, giving you these four

00:02:40.740 --> 00:02:46.980
probabilities. And because probabilities should sum to one, the four numbers in the output

00:02:46.980 --> 00:02:53.980
y hat, they should sum to one. The standard model for getting a neural network to do this

00:02:54.020 --> 00:02:59.540
uses what's called a softmax layer in the output layer in order to generate these outputs.

00:02:59.540 --> 00:03:03.380
Let me write down the map and we can come back and get some intuition about what the

00:03:03.380 --> 00:03:09.860
softmax layer is doing. So the final layer of the neural network, you are going to compute

00:03:09.940 --> 00:03:16.940
as usual, the linear part of the layer, so z capital L, that's the z variable for the

00:03:16.940 --> 00:03:23.940
final layer. So remember, this is layer capital L. So as usual, you compute that as WL times

00:03:25.220 --> 00:03:32.220
the activation of the previous layer, plus the biases for that final layer. Now having

00:03:32.500 --> 00:03:38.940
computed z, you now need to apply what's called the softmax activation function. So

00:03:38.940 --> 00:03:45.540
the activation function is a bit unusual for the softmax layer, but this is what it does.

00:03:45.540 --> 00:03:52.540
First we're going to compute a temporary variable, which we call t, which is e to the zL. So

00:03:54.740 --> 00:04:00.740
this is applied element wise. So zL here, in our example, zL is going to be four by

00:04:00.740 --> 00:04:07.740
one is a four dimensional vector. So t itself, e to the zL, that's an element wise exponentiation.

00:04:08.540 --> 00:04:15.540
t will also be a four by one dimensional vector. Then the output, aL, is going to be basically

00:04:17.900 --> 00:04:24.900
the vector t, but normalized to sum to one. So aL is going to be e to the zL divided by

00:04:26.260 --> 00:04:33.260
sum from j equals one through four, because we have four classes of t subscript i. So

00:04:34.260 --> 00:04:41.260
another way of saying this is that aL is also a four by one vector, and the i-th element

00:04:43.020 --> 00:04:47.780
of this four dimensional vector, let's write that aL subscript i, this is going to be equal

00:04:47.780 --> 00:04:54.780
to t i over sum of t i. In case this math isn't clear, we'll do an example in a minute,

00:04:54.780 --> 00:05:01.780
that'll make this clearer. So in case this math isn't clear, let's go through a specific

00:05:04.940 --> 00:05:11.940
example that will make this clearer. Let's say that you've computed zL, and zL is a four

00:05:12.420 --> 00:05:19.300
dimensional vector. Let's say it's five, two, negative one, three. What we're going to

00:05:19.300 --> 00:05:24.580
do is use this element wise exponentiation to compute this vector t. So t is going to

00:05:24.580 --> 00:05:30.580
be e to the five, e to the two, e to the negative one, e to the three. And if you plug

00:05:30.580 --> 00:05:35.820
that into the calculator, these are the values you get. e to the five is one four eight, one

00:05:35.820 --> 00:05:42.500
four, e squared is about seven point four, e to the negative one is 0.4, and e cubed

00:05:42.500 --> 00:05:49.500
is 20.1. And so the way we go from the vector t to the vector aL is to just normalize these

00:05:50.500 --> 00:05:57.500
entries to sum to one. So if you sum up the elements of t, if you just add up those four

00:05:57.900 --> 00:06:04.900
numbers, you get one seven six point three. So finally, aL is just going to be this vector

00:06:09.100 --> 00:06:16.100
t as a vector divided by one seven six point three. So for example, this first note here,

00:06:16.580 --> 00:06:23.580
this will output e to the five divided by one seven six point three, and that turns out to

00:06:23.580 --> 00:06:30.580
be 0.842. So saying that for this image, if this is the value of z you get, the chance

00:06:30.900 --> 00:06:37.900
of it being called zero is 84.2%. And then the next note outputs e squared over one seven

00:06:38.900 --> 00:06:45.900
six point three, that turns out to be 0.042. So this is the value of z. So this is the

00:06:46.100 --> 00:06:53.100
value of z is 4.2% chance. The next one is e to the negative one over that, which is 0.02.

00:06:56.700 --> 00:07:03.700
And the final one is e cubed over that, which is 0.114. So by the 11.4% chance that this

00:07:07.380 --> 00:07:11.420
is class number three, which I guess is the baby kid class, right? So there's a chance

00:07:11.420 --> 00:07:18.060
of it being class zero, class one, class two, class three. So the output of the neural network

00:07:18.060 --> 00:07:25.060
aL, this is also y hat, this is a four by one vector, where the elements of this four

00:07:25.460 --> 00:07:32.460
by one vector are going to be these four numbers that we just computed. So this algorithm takes

00:07:33.100 --> 00:07:40.100
the vector zL and maps it to four probabilities that sum to one. And if we summarize what

00:07:41.100 --> 00:07:47.780
we just did to map from zL to aL, this whole computation computing the exponentiation to

00:07:47.780 --> 00:07:54.780
get this temporary variable t, and then normalizing, we can summarize this into a softmax activation

00:07:55.460 --> 00:08:02.460
function and say aL equals the activation function g applied to the vector zL. The unusual thing

00:08:04.560 --> 00:08:09.260
about this particular activation function is that this activation function g, it takes

00:08:09.340 --> 00:08:16.340
this input a four by one vector and it outputs a four by one vector. So previously our activation

00:08:16.500 --> 00:08:21.260
functions used to take in a single real value input. So for example, the sigmoid and the

00:08:21.260 --> 00:08:26.420
value activation functions input that real number and output a real number. The unusual

00:08:26.420 --> 00:08:31.340
thing about the softmax activation function is because it needs to normalize across the

00:08:31.340 --> 00:08:35.060
different possible outputs, it needs to take in a vector of inputs and then outputs

00:08:35.060 --> 00:08:39.980
a vector. So what are the things that a softmax classifier can represent? I'm going to show

00:08:39.980 --> 00:08:46.980
you some examples where you have inputs x1, x2, and these feed directly to a softmax layer

00:08:48.180 --> 00:08:54.220
that has three or four or more output nodes that then outputs y hat. So I'm going to show

00:08:54.220 --> 00:09:01.220
you a neural network with no hidden layer and all it does is compute z1 equals w1 times

00:09:02.220 --> 00:09:09.220
the input x plus b and then the output a1 or y hat is just a softmax activation function

00:09:12.140 --> 00:09:17.020
applied to z1. So in this neural network with no hidden layer, it should give you a sense

00:09:17.020 --> 00:09:21.980
of the types of things a softmax function can represent. So here's one example with

00:09:21.980 --> 00:09:28.980
just raw inputs x1 and x2, a softmax layer with c equals three output classes can represent

00:09:29.500 --> 00:09:34.060
this type of decision boundary. Now this is kind of a several linear decision boundaries,

